# Compound plan

A good plan makes the work boring: an agent with no other context can execute it step by step.

## Research before writing

1. The PRD entry: feature ID, acceptance criteria, business rules.
2. `docs/solutions/`: lessons for this module or similar features (avoid repeating past mistakes).
3. Existing code: the closest similar feature; reuse its patterns, components and helpers.
4. Docs for the pinned versions of any library you will use (do not rely on memory for APIs).
5. Shared knowledge from other projects: run `python <skill>/scripts/learn.py suggest <topic words>`. Prefer a **proven** entry, note its id under "Lessons applied", and explain in one line why it is the best fit (or why you chose otherwise). `AUTOMATION_STATUS.md` names the automation skill folder; if that folder exists on this machine, `<skill>/scripts/learn.py` is available. If not, skip these steps.

## Plan file

Path: `docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-<feature-id>-<short-slug>.md`

```markdown
# <Feature ID> <Title>
Status: Draft | Approved | In progress | Done

## Goal
One paragraph; link PRD section.

## Acceptance criteria
AC1 … (copied from PRD) → test that will prove it

## Approach
Data changes · API changes (method, path, roles, tier) · UI changes (panel, route, components) · jobs/integrations

## Files to touch
- path — why (new/changed)

## Security
Auth decision · roles · ownership rule · validation · rate tier · CAPTCHA · audit log · new attack surface

## Risks and mitigations
Migrations, concurrency, performance (indexes, N+1), backwards compatibility

## Tasks
- [ ] 1. Small, verifiable step (one commit each)
- [ ] 2. …

## Lessons applied
Links to docs/solutions entries used
```

## Rules

- Tasks are small (one commit, under ~30 minutes each) and ordered so the build stays green after each.
- Tests are written in the same task as the code they test, or before it.
- If the plan changes the schema or shared packages, mark it **serial** (no parallel work on those files).
- Run `compound-analysis` on the plan, then set Status: Approved.
